   331	
   332	0
   333	     Successful completion.
   334	
   335	1
   336	     Invalid command, invalid syntax, invalid regular expression or a
   337	     GNU ‘sed’ extension command used with ‘--posix’.
   338	
   339	2
   340	     One or more of the input file specified on the command line could
   341	     not be opened (e.g.  if a file is not found, or read permission is
   342	     denied).  Processing continued with other files.
   343	
   344	4
   345	     An I/O error, or a serious processing error during runtime, GNU
   346	     ‘sed’ aborted immediately.
   347	
   348	   Additionally, the commands ‘q’ and ‘Q’ can be used to terminate ‘sed’
   349	with a custom exit code value (this is a GNU ‘sed’ extension):
   350	

